<title>
Inspection of Power Window Main Switch and Its Circuits
</title>
<servinfosub id = "AENLSB0A9504005001">
<title>
Voltage Check
</title>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove door trim and power window main switch. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A9506008"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Connect connector to power window main switch and set ignition “ON”.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Initialize power window system. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A9506018"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Check voltage using circuit tester.
</ptxt>
<attention3>
<list1 type = "unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>
Check that battery voltage is 12 V or more.
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Measure power window main switch with power window lock switch “OFF”.
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Outputs from terminals marked with asterisk (*1) cannot be measured with voltmeter because they are pulse signals. Use oscilloscope for measuring these outputs.
</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</attention3>
